Space Arenas is free to play, free to change and free to share — and it must stay that
way. You may do anything with this game, including publishing your own modified version,
as long as nothing is ever sold and the credits and this license stay in place.

This is a source-available, non-commercial license. It is deliberately NOT an OSI-approved
open-source license, because it forbids commercial use.

In short (this summary is not part of the terms — the terms below govern):
  * Play it, study it, change anything, share it with anyone.
  * Every version stays free: no price, no paid access, no ads, no donations required.
  * Keep the copyright notice and this LICENSE file with every copy.
  * The name, logo, sprites and music stay with the author. Use them in the game, in your
    free versions, and in your own non-commercial projects with credit — never sell them,
    and never pass the name or logo off as your own.
  * Say it is a modified version, and let your users keep the same freedoms.

1. Definitions

   "Game" means the Space Arenas software in this repository: the source code, the built
   client and LAN host, the shared libraries, the game data, the map builder, the website,
   and the documentation.

   "Assets" means the Space Arenas name and logo, all sprite and artwork files (including
   the .png sprite sheets and HUD art), all sound and music files (including the lobby
   track SPACE.ARENAS_by_SDEVRAMI.mp3 and the .wav effects), and any other graphics, audio
   or branding shipped with the Game.

   "Modified Version" means any work based on or derived from the Game, including forks,
   patches, ports, translations, rebalances, asset edits and re-uploads.

   "Distribute" means to give, send, upload, host, publish, mirror or otherwise make
   available to anyone else.

   "Free of Charge" means no money changes hands for access: no price, licence fee,
   subscription, in-app purchase, donation requirement, paywalled download, advertising,
   or any other monetisation attached to using or getting the Game.

   "You" means the person or group exercising the rights below.

2. What you may do

   You may use, copy, run, modify, merge, combine, translate, rebalance, port and
   Distribute the Game and Modified Versions, Free of Charge, for personal and
   non-commercial purposes, provided you meet the conditions in sections 3 and 4.

   This includes the normal reasons people fork a game: fixing bugs, adding units, maps,
   modes, languages, graphics, tools, servers and quality-of-life changes, and publishing
   those changes for everyone.

3. Conditions — every version stays free

   a) Free of Charge. You may not sell, rent, sublicense for payment, or otherwise charge
      for the Game or for a Modified Version, and you may not require payment, a
      subscription, a donation or watching ads to download, access or play it.

   b) Keep the notice and this license. Every copy and every Modified Version you
      Distribute must include this LICENSE file unmodified and the copyright notice above.
      If you distribute source code, these must be kept in the source too.

   c) Say that you changed it. A Modified Version must clearly state that it is modified
      and is not the official Space Arenas release, and must not imply that it was made or
      endorsed by the original author.

   d) Pass on the same terms. Everyone who receives the Game or a Modified Version from
      you receives the same rights and the same limits under this license. You may not
      relicense a Modified Version on terms that would allow charging money for it.

4. Assets and the project name

   a) Ownership. The Assets remain the property of the copyright holder. This license
      grants you permission to use them inside the Game — it does not transfer ownership
      of them to you.

   b) Inside the game. You may use and modify the Assets as part of the Game and as part
      of a Modified Version that stays Free of Charge under section 3. Editing sprites,
      remixing the music or replacing art in your own version is allowed.

   c) In your own projects. You may also use the Assets in an unrelated project of your
      own, as long as that project is Free of Charge in the sense of section 3 and you
      credit the original author where a user can reasonably find it (an about screen, a
      credits list or a readme) — for example "Sprites and music from Space Arenas by
      SDevRami". You may not sell the Assets, charge for access to a project that uses
      them, or ship them in a paid product, a paid asset pack, a paid store listing or
      merchandise.

   d) The name and logo. You may not use the "Space Arenas" name or logo as the name of
      your own project or version, or in any way that suggests it is the official release
      or is endorsed by the original author. A credit such as
      "«Your Title» — based on Space Arenas" is welcome and encouraged.

   e) Contributions. By submitting a change to this repository you agree that your
      contribution is licensed under this license, and you confirm you have the right to
      submit it — including any code, artwork, sound or music you add.

5. What is not permitted

   Commercial use of the Game, of a Modified Version, or of the Assets is not permitted.
   That includes selling the game or its code, bundling it into a paid product, charging
   for hosting or access, distributing it with advertising or sponsorships, and running it
   as a paid service. If you want to use Space Arenas commercially, contact the copyright
   holder for separate written permission.

6. No warranty

   The Game is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, express or implied,
   including but not limited to the warranties of merchantability, fitness for a
   particular purpose, title and non-infringement. The copyright holder does not warrant
   that the Game will work correctly, be free of bugs or be fit for any purpose. You use
   it at your own risk.

7. Limitation of liability

   To the maximum extent permitted by law, the copyright holder and contributors are not
   liable for any claim, damage or other liability — including lost data, lost saves or
   lost time — whether in an action of contract, tort or otherwise, arising from, out of
   or in connection with the Game or its use. Because the Game is provided free of charge,
   this liability is limited to the amount you paid for it, which is zero.

8. Termination

   Your rights under this license end automatically if you break any of its terms, for
   example by selling the Game or by removing the credits. They are restored if you stop
   breaking them and come back into compliance. Sections 6 and 7 survive termination.

